# Calibration and sensor processing (lib/opensc2/cal_store.c and friends), sourced from Kconfig.

config OPENSC2_CAL
	bool "Calibration: the cal/ keys, the calibration commands and raw inputs"
	default y
	help
	  As on the real controller: the calibration keys (cal/joy_l, cal/joy_r, cal/trg_l,
	  cal/trg_r, cal/prs_l, cal/prs_r, cal/touch_l, cal/touch_r, cal/rgbw_r/_g/_b/_w,
	  cal/volt_offset, cal/sensors/gyroscope/bias) kept under "opensc2/cal/" in Zephyr settings,
	  read with vendor command 0xED and changed with 0xEE, 0xEF and 0xF0; the factory recordings
	  0xD8 (sticks), 0xC0 (triggers) and 0xC3 (pad pressure); 0xE2 (save one side) and 0xFE
	  (erase every cal/ key, only with its key). A factory reset (0x86) keeps them.

	  Raw inputs (opensc2_set_stick_raw() and friends, <opensc2/cal.h>): the library applies the
	  stored calibration and controller settings 30, 31, 34, 35, 46, 52, 53, 60 and 62 to raw ADC
	  counts, pressure and capacitive words at every state report, as the real controller does,
	  and the recordings take their samples from them. An application that gives finished values
	  only is not affected. About 400 bytes of RAM.

if OPENSC2_CAL

config OPENSC2_CAL_PRESSURE_CLICK
	bool "Raw pad pressure also sets the pad's click bit"
	default y
	help
	  As on the real controller, which has no click switch under its pads: the click follows the
	  calibrated pressure (settings 52 and 53, 8 points of hysteresis) while the pad is touched.
	  Turn off on a board whose pads have a click switch of their own and also report pressure.

config OPENSC2_CAL_STICK_DEAD_ZONE
	int "Centre dead zone of raw sticks, report units (0: none, as the real controller)"
	default 0
	range 0 16383
	help
	  Per axis: a calibrated value up to this reads 0, the rest is stretched back to full scale.
	  The real controller has none (its Hall sticks do not drift); potentiometer sticks may want
	  about 2000 (6 %).

config OPENSC2_CAL_STICK_GROW_RANGE
	bool "Raw sticks: let the range grow past the stored extremes (July 2026's rule)"
	help
	  July 2026's controller firmware let each half's outer end follow a low-pass copy of the
	  reading (factor 0.15) past the stored extreme, in RAM only; October keeps the stored range.

endif # OPENSC2_CAL

config OPENSC2_PAD_RULES
	bool "Pad rotation (settings 2 and 24) and stabiliser (setting 80 = 2) on the reported pads"
	default y
	depends on OPENSC2_CAL
	help
	  After the hardware test hooks' injection, as the real controller processes its pads: with
	  settings 2 and 24 both non-zero the pads' positions turn by setting 2's angle (the left pad
	  the other way), and with setting 80 = 2 the touch stabiliser holds a new touch still until
	  the thumb moves more than 4369 units. Both are off with the default settings (2 = 0,
	  80 = 1), so nothing changes until a host writes them. Report 0x42 and lizard mode see the
	  result.
